---
const faqs = [
	{
		q: 'How does pi-rs relate to upstream pi?',
		a: 'pi-rs is a Rust port of the pi coding agent. It keeps upstream’s model, tool and session semantics — including the wire format — so behaviour you depend on does not change when you swap binaries.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Which providers can I use?',
		a: 'Ten wire APIs ship in the box: OpenAI chat completions and responses, ChatGPT Codex, Anthropic messages, Gemini, Vertex, Azure OpenAI, Amazon Bedrock Converse, Mistral conversations and the pi-messages gateway. Eight OAuth sign-in flows are supported, and any OpenAI-compatible endpoint can be added through models.json.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Will my existing sessions and MCP servers keep working?',
		a: 'Yes. Sessions are stored as JSONL in upstream’s tree format and stay readable in both directions. Project-level .pi resources — skills, prompt templates, extensions and mcp.json — are discovered by both binaries; only the user-level config directory differs (~/.pi-rs/agent).',
	},
	{
		q: 'Do I need Node installed?',
		a: 'No. pi-rs is a single Rust binary with no runtime dependencies. Node is only required if you write an extension, because extensions run as external processes.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What can I extend?',
		a: 'Skills, prompt templates, external extension processes and installable packages. Extensions can register tools, add slash commands, subscribe to session and turn events, intercept tool calls and drive the TUI through a UI bridge.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What happens when the context fills up?',
		a: 'pi-rs compacts automatically once the context crosses your threshold, splits over-long turns with a double summary, and recovers from an overflow by dropping the failed turn, choosing a cut point, compacting and retrying once.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Is it ready to use?',
		a: 'It is v0.1 and moving fast — the framework, providers, tools, MCP, sessions and RPC surface are all in place, while SSH environments and a few deferred provider flags are still on the roadmap. Everything is MIT licensed.',
	},
];
---

<section class="section faq" id="faq">
	<div class="container faq__inner">
		<div class="faq__head reveal">
			<span class="eyebrow">FAQ</span>
			<h2>Questions, answered</h2>
			<p>Something missing? The README and the docs folder in the repository go deeper on every topic below.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="faq__list reveal">
			{
				faqs.map((faq) => (
					<details class="faq__item">
						<summary>
							{faq.q}
							<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
								<path d="M3 6l5 5 5-5" />
							</svg>
						</summary>
						<p>{faq.a}</p>
					</details>
				))
			}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.faq {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.faq__inner {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
		gap: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
		align-items: start;
	}

	.faq__head h2 {
		font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.2vw, 2.5rem);
		margin-block: 0.85rem 0.9rem;
	}

	.faq__head p {
		color: var(--text-muted);
		font-size: 0.95rem;
	}

	.faq__list {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.6rem;
	}

	.faq__item {
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: var(--surface);
		overflow: hidden;
		transition:
			border-color 0.25s var(--ease),
			background-color 0.25s var(--ease);
	}

	.faq__item[open] {
		border-color: var(--border-strong);
		background: var(--surface-strong);
	}

	.faq__item summary {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 1.05rem 1.25rem;
		cursor: pointer;
		font-weight: 550;
		font-size: 0.98rem;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.faq__item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}

	.faq__item summary svg {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		color: var(--text-dim);
		transition: transform 0.25s var(--ease);
	}

	.faq__item[open] summary svg {
		transform: rotate(180deg);
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	.faq__item p {
		padding: 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
		color: var(--text-muted);
		font-size: 0.93rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		.faq__inner {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
